 "title": "IL300 linear optocoupler with servo and output photodiodes, K3 bins D to G (IL300-DEFG), DIP-8 and SMD-8",
 "source": {
  "document": "83622",
  "revision": "Rev. 2.8, 17-Jul-2026",
  "pages": 8
 },
 "summary": "An analog optocoupler: one AlGaAs infrared LED lights two matched PIN photodiodes. The servo photodiode (pins 3, 4) sits on the LED side and its current IP1 is fed back to hold the LED's light output steady against its own nonlinearity, ageing and temperature; the output photodiode (pins 5, 6) sits across the barrier and its current IP2 follows the same light. The ratio K3 = K2/K1 of the two gains is therefore stable, typically ±0.005 %/°C, and the parts are sorted by K3 into letter bins; IL300-DEFG ships from bins D, E, F and G only (K3 0.765 to 1.181). Isolation is 4420 VRMS for one minute; bandwidth is 1.4 MHz typical.",
 "key_figures": [
  [
   "Transfer gain K3 = K2/K1",
   "0.56 min, 1 typ, 1.65 max; IL300-DEFG 0.765 to 1.181"
  ],
  [
   "Servo gain K1 and forward gain K2",
   "0.005 min, 0.009 typ, 0.015 max at IF = 10 mA, Vdet = -15 V"
  ],
  [
   "Transfer gain stability",
   "± 0.005 %/°C typ, ± 0.15 %/°C max, 0 °C to 75 °C"
  ],
  [
